{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["And Moses said to Aaron and to Eleazar and to Ithamar. He turned his face toward Aaron and spoke with him mouth to mouth, therefore it is written אל אהרן, but he did not turn his face toward Eleazar and Ithamar, therefore אל is not said of them." "<b>ולאיתמר בניו</b> — a break, to say that they too were worthy, except that the decree was interrupted from them. And this is what is stated at Sinai: 'and the priests, YHWH, the priests' — these are Aaron and his four sons, except that in the merit of Aaron they were saved." "<b>תפרעו</b> — 2. אל תפרעו and the other ושמעו מוסר וחכמו ואל תפרעו — because they did not heed reproof and let their hair grow loose, for they ruled in the presence of their master, or they brought alien fire, causing the survivors to be commanded אל תפרעו." "<b>ועל כל העדה יקצוף</b> — because they were public emissaries, and a ש\"צ who errs is a bad sign for his senders. 'And your brothers, the whole house of Israel, shall mourn the burning' — שת\"ח: when one dies, all become his relatives."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {2 "Reading ופרעו (let grow loose) as part of the linkage; the word play between תפרעו and פרעו is preserved as written."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:12.662243947Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}